 {"q": "What does God say to Cain before the murder, and why does it matter?", "options": ["Nothing; Cain acts without warning", "That sin is crouching at the door but Cain can rule over it, showing that Cain was free and responsible", "That Cain is cursed already", "That Abel deserves to die"], "answer": 1, "why": "Genesis insists that wrongdoing is a choice, not a fate."},
